From 5ccb041b986ebe1ee23720652ffeb591536982cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 10:52:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/31] a210: sync A210-specific sources to validated vendor
 branch

The kernel/patches/*.patch snapshot used to bootstrap this branch predates
substantial A210 rework that landed on the vendor branch osl/a210-v2.9.0 -- the
tree we validated on hardware this cycle (console, networking, AON firmware,
RTC, reboot and poweroff all working). The stale snapshot notably carried an
older power-domain topology (power_can/power_pwm vs the reworked power_peri2 /
A210_PD_PERI2) and an older a210-pd.c clk sequence (clk_bulk_enable +
early reset-deassert vs clk_bulk_prepare_enable + late deassert).

Overwrite the 27 A210-specific sources that drifted with their verbatim
content from osl/a210-v2.9.0. These files do not exist in upstream v6.6.141,
so there is no stable-base context to preserve; taking them whole keeps the
DTS, power/reset bindings and zhihe drivers mutually consistent and identical
to the validated tree. The DTS Makefile keeps its 'dtb-y += a210-dev.dtb' trim
(we ship only a210-dev). Modified-upstream files are left as the patch subset
produced them; the boot test is the gate for those.

Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>

v7.0 port: kept upstream drivers/iommu/riscv/iommu-platform.c (the vendor
riscv-iommu was dropped for the upstreamed one in the group-10 pick; the
A210 zhihe,iommu node is disabled).

Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
